# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production frontend configuration
#
# Vite loads this file automatically for `npm run build` (mode: production) and
# for `npm run preview`. It is NOT loaded by `npm run dev`, so editing it
# cannot break anybody's local setup.
#
# This file is committed on purpose - it is public configuration, not a secret.
# Every VITE_ variable ends up readable in the shipped bundle anyway, and the
# deployed API's address is not something the browser could be kept from
# knowing. The secrets policy is unchanged: nothing confidential goes in any
# file under frontend/. See .env.example.
#
# A shell variable overrides this file, which is how a build for a different
# backend is made without editing it:
#     VITE_API_BASE_URL="https://other-host/api/v1/" npm run build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The deployed Django REST API on Railway, including the version prefix and a
# trailing slash. Verified live at .../api/v1/health/.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://legalmetrology-compliance-production.up.railway.app/api/v1/
